cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  State-of-Charge Estimation for EV Lithium-Ion Batteries: A Controlled
  Comparison of Deep Learning Architectures on the LG 18650HG2 Cell
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Farhad
    family-names: Bagheri
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/FarhadBagheri23/SoC-Estimation-EV-Batteries-LSTM
abstract: >-
  A battery management system reports State of Charge but cannot measure it
  directly; it infers SoC by integrating current, so any current-sensor error
  accumulates rather than averaging away. This work compares six SoC
  estimators on the LG 18650HG2 benchmark across -20 to +40 degrees C under
  one data pipeline, one training procedure and comparable parameter budgets,
  with every architecture trained three times so that a design difference can
  be separated from initialisation variance. The two leading architectures
  are separated by less than the spread across seeds and are reported as
  tied.
keywords:
  - state of charge
  - lithium-ion battery
  - LSTM
  - deep learning
  - state of charge estimation
  - battery management system
  - electric vehicles
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-08-02'
